# Ontology Framework Development Rules

## Project Context
This is an ontology framework project focusing on semantic data modeling and knowledge representation.

## Code Style Requirements
- Always use descriptive variable names that reflect ontological concepts
- Add inline comments explaining semantic relationships
- Include type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Use docstrings that explain the ontological purpose of each function

## Naming Conventions
- Classes: PascalCase with ontology domain prefix (e.g., `OntologyEntity`, `SemanticRelation`)
- Functions: snake_case with action verbs (e.g., `create_entity`, `validate_relationship`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `DEFAULT_NAMESPACE`, `SCHEMA_VERSION`)
- Files: snake_case with descriptive names (e.g., `entity_manager.py`, `relationship_validator.py`)

## AI Instructions
When generating code for this project:
1. Always start function names with "onto_model_" as a prefix (this will help us verify if this rule is being read)
2. Include a comment "# Generated following ontology framework rules" at the top of each code block
3. Suggest using RDF/OWL terminology in variable names when appropriate
4. Prioritize semantic clarity over brevity in naming

## Testing Requirements
- Write unit tests for all ontology validation functions
- Include edge cases for malformed semantic data
- Test namespace resolution and URI validation

## Documentation Standards
- Document all ontological assumptions
- Include examples of expected RDF triples
- Explain semantic relationships in plain English
